{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03302",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.73,
      "end_seconds": 8.79,
      "duration_seconds": 8.06,
      "text": "Yeah, uh, hello doctor, sorry, I took a wrong turn on the way here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.85,
      "end_seconds": 15.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.92,
      "text": "Yes, come in and and sit down. What brings you here today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 17.62,
      "end_seconds": 23.19,
      "duration_seconds": 5.57,
      "text": "So the thing is, I've got bloating when I slip up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 24.37,
      "end_seconds": 27.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "what do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.12,
      "end_seconds": 50.18,
      "duration_seconds": 22.06,
      "text": "Right, you know, I'm on Seretide inhaler, twice a day. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it. I'd been on Asthalin inhaler, not any more though, I stopped."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.99,
      "end_seconds": 54.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "What's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.66,
      "end_seconds": 60.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.84,
      "text": "Mm, it's been going on for about three months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 62.22,
      "end_seconds": 67.22,
      "duration_seconds": 5.0,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 71.82,
      "end_seconds": 96.14,
      "duration_seconds": 24.32,
      "text": "Gluten definitely sets it off. Mostly moderate. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't. I took the morning off to come in today. I've had mouth ulcers too, for ten days. Well, you know, as for mouth ulcers, it's mild, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.69,
      "end_seconds": 101.86,
      "duration_seconds": 5.17,
      "text": "What about a rash on your elbows, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.25,
      "end_seconds": 104.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "yes, actually"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.48,
      "end_seconds": 113.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "Have you had any vomiting, weight loss or diarrhoea?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.25,
      "end_seconds": 116.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "Nope, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.24,
      "end_seconds": 123.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "And bone pain, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.78,
      "end_seconds": 126.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "Nope, no bone pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.89,
      "end_seconds": 131.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "okay, any trouble with the waterworks?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 133.5,
      "end_seconds": 138.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "Mm, that's normal as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.84,
      "end_seconds": 162.11,
      "duration_seconds": 5.27,
      "text": "tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.72,
      "end_seconds": 178.82,
      "duration_seconds": 15.1,
      "text": "I'll have a glass of wine with dinner. I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day. I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.59,
      "end_seconds": 191.71,
      "duration_seconds": 4.12,
      "text": "Any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 192.76,
      "end_seconds": 198.51,
      "duration_seconds": 5.75,
      "text": "Okay, so yes, kiwi, it gives me an itchy mouth."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.57,
      "end_seconds": 203.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "Tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.45,
      "end_seconds": 212.1,
      "duration_seconds": 7.65,
      "text": "yes, asthma a neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.76,
      "end_seconds": 215.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "Let me take your readings now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.29,
      "end_seconds": 231.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.07,
      "end_seconds": 248.94,
      "duration_seconds": 6.87,
      "text": "okay: BP is 115 over 78, SpO2 99 percent on room air, heart rate 79."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 250.32,
      "end_seconds": 252.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "Is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.33,
      "end_seconds": 256.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "We'll look at it together shortly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.51,
      "end_seconds": 294.06,
      "duration_seconds": 20.55,
      "text": "right, here's what I'm thinking. It points towards coeliac disease on a gluten-free diet with some accidental exposure. I can't rule out iron deficiency yet. I'm sending you for coeliac antibodies because of coeliac follow-up. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 295.82,
      "end_seconds": 297.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.21,
      "text": "Mm, alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.67,
      "end_seconds": 306.82,
      "duration_seconds": 8.15,
      "text": "Check labels carefully and use separate toasters and chopping boards. I'll also refer you to the dietitian."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 308.39,
      "end_seconds": 309.09,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.79,
      "end_seconds": 321.39,
      "duration_seconds": 10.6,
      "text": "If it hasn't settled in two weeks, we'd think about a blood count, but not now. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 322.39,
      "end_seconds": 327.5,
      "duration_seconds": 5.11,
      "text": "Right, uh, I'll do that. Thank you, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 329.45,
      "end_seconds": 330.71,
      "duration_seconds": 1.26,
      "text": "All the best."
    }
  ]
}